   "text": "I read the drawing as the cyclic peptide H-Cpa-cyclo[D-Cys-Tyr-D-Phe(4-ureidomethyl)-Lys-Thr-Cys]-D-Tyr-NH2, with a disulfide between the two Cys side chains.\n\nThe residues, from the N-terminus:\n1. **Cpa** is 4-chlorophenylalanine with a free NH2. From the hashed NH2 bond I worked out an S centre, so it is the L form.\n2. **D-Cys** has a wedged N bond and works out to S, which is D for cysteine. Its CH2\u2013S forms the disulfide.\n3. **Tyr** is L, with the wedged CH2 on the alpha carbon.\n4. **D-Phe(4-ureidomethyl)** carries CH2NHC(=O)NH2 at the para position of the ring. I took the D configuration from the name rather than re-deriving it from the wedge.\n5. **Lys** is L, with a free (CH2)4NH2 side chain.\n6. **Thr** is L, (2S,3R), with the beta OH.\n7. **Cys** is L, and its sulfur closes the disulfide to residue 2.\n8. **D-Tyr-NH2** is the C-terminal primary amide.\n\nIn the SMILES, the disulfide is written with ring-closure label %10 on the two sulfurs.\n\nSMILES: N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(Cl)cc1)C(=O)N[C@H](CS%10)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(O)cc2)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc3ccc(CNC(N)=O)cc3)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CS%10)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc4ccc(O)cc4)C(N)=O"
  }
